{"topic overlaps": ["Quark Mass Anomalous Dimension", "Operator Product Expansion (OPE)", "Chiral Symmetry Restoration", "Highly Excited Hadrons", "Renormalization Group Equations", "Perturbative Corrections", "Regge Trajectories", "Decay Constants", "Vector and Axial-Vector Mesons", "Hadronic Resonances"], "question": "How does the restoration of chiral symmetry in highly excited hadrons affect the mass splittings and decay constants of vector and axial-vector mesons, and what are the implications for the operator product expansion (OPE) in the context of QCD?", "answer": "The restoration of chiral symmetry in highly excited hadrons implies that the mass splittings between vector and axial-vector mesons, which are chiral partners, should decrease as the excitation number increases. This is because the effects of spontaneous chiral symmetry breaking, which are significant for low-lying states, become less important at higher energies. The decay constants of these mesons, which are also affected by chiral symmetry breaking, should similarly approach each other as the excitation number grows. In the context of the operator product expansion (OPE), this means that the contributions from the chiral symmetry breaking terms in the OPE should diminish, leading to a more symmetric behavior of the spectral densities of the vector and axial-vector currents. This is consistent with the expectation that the OPE, which is valid at high energies, should reflect the underlying symmetries of the QCD Lagrangian.", "usageJudgementGeneratorLLM": ["hep-ph/9703278", "0803.3625", "hep-ph/0201242", "hep-ph/9608480", "hep-ph/0507246"], "papersInputtedForGeneration": [{"ArXiv": "hep-ph/9703278", "category": "hep-ph", "cosineSimilarity": 0.8737865561483422}, {"ArXiv": "0803.3625", "category": "hep-ph", "cosineSimilarity": null}, {"ArXiv": "hep-ph/0201242", "category": "hep-ph", "cosineSimilarity": 0.8816896862090561}, {"ArXiv": "hep-ph/9608480", "category": "hep-ph", "cosineSimilarity": 0.89